An agent file's model: field is now honoured, so model: haiku actually runs on Haiku instead of being silently ignored. Build, the full cargo test run (0 failures), clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all pass. It's committed as f05f9b3d and I commented on #1250.

How the model is picked. One function, choose_agent_model in src/agent_dispatch.rs, decides for both the agent tool and the yoyo agents listing, so they can't disagree. The order is: the file's model:, then sub_agent_model, then the main model.
• `inherit` means the main model, even when sub_agent_model is set.
• `haiku`, `sonnet`, `opus`, `fable` (any case; that's the alias list on Claude Code's docs page): with provider = "anthropic", they run on the main model's exact id if it's the same family. Otherwise they run on the newest model of that family in yoagent's preset list, so I never typed an id.
• On any other provider, an alias or a claude-… id is never sent, because it would fail every call. The agent runs on sub_agent_model or the main model instead, and its answer starts with a note naming both models and the reason, so the calling model can tell the user.
• Any other id is sent as written, so llama3.1 on ollama works.

The `yoyo agents` listing now reads --provider, --model and the config file the way a session does. I ran the built binary on a temp project and got all three row shapes:
• model: haiku → claude-haiku-5-5 (the newest preset)
• model: haiku (falls back to deepseek-v4-pro: ...) with --provider deepseek
• model: haiku → claude-haiku-4-5 with --model claude-haiku-4-5 (the same-family rule)

Tests. The new tests failed before the implementation existed and pass now. They cover each rule, including model_field_is_honoured_not_disclaimed, plus two inputs that must be sent as written: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6 on openrouter and haiku-local:7b on ollama. One test checks the note actually reaches the parent's answer. To prove that test can fail, I disabled the note in one atomic edit: it failed by name, then passed once restored, with no marker left behind.

Other changes. I added config::configured_sub_agent_model(), because the existing helper can't tell "not set" from "set to the main model", and inherit needs that difference. The "not honoured yet" wording is gone from src and docs. docs/src/usage/commands.md now documents the order and the fallback, and both ARCHITECTURE.md entries mark the old claims as superseded.

One limit I haven't decided: a custom OpenAI-compatible provider that serves Claude under claude-… ids will now fall back for those ids. I noted this in ARCHITECTURE.md and on #1250. It's a small rule change if someone hits it.

Next: milestone 4 (a /doctor row for skipped and duplicate agent files, plus the docs page). #1255 is still open for per-row status in yoyo agents and the note that explains a refusal at run time.
